From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] List style for the connection editor, modem details, sound
 and fast charging

Plinius: the pages of the connection editor (a saved Wi-Fi network, a
VPN, WireGuard) look like the other pages of Settings, rows in boxed
lists in an AdwPreferencesPage instead of grids with labels left of
the fields; nothing scrolls sideways any more, so the back swipe works
on IPv4 and IPv6 as well:

- Details: the facts as rows (title, the value below), the options as
  switch rows, "Forget" as a button row of its own.
- Identity: entry rows; BSSID, MAC and cloned MAC offer what the combo
  boxes offered in a menu at the end of the row.
- IPv4/IPv6: the method as rows with a check button, each address and
  route a boxed list of entry rows (ce-plinius-ip-row.c, a whole file
  copied in prepare(), validates them like CEIPAddressEntry and
  CENetmaskEntry), DNS, search domains and routes as groups.
- Security: the type as a combo row; WPA & WPA2 / WPA3 Personal as a
  password row bound to libnma's field, so validating and saving stay
  libnma's; the other types keep libnma's form, in one column.
- VPN: the name as an entry row; the plugin's form (and its dialogs
  shown as pages, OpenVPN's "Advanced…") turned into boxed lists, one
  row per label and field, rows following the plugin's visibility and
  sensitivity.
- WireGuard: groups of entry, password, spin and switch rows, a row per
  peer, the peer editor as a form page instead of a popover. "Add peer
  routes" is saved now, fwmark values above 2^31 no longer get cut.
- Modem details: the title of each row as on the other pages, the value
  below it; with "property" both were dimmed.
- Sound: no level bar next to "Test…" (it looked like a button without
  a function); the speaker test wheel stays a circle instead of
  stretching over the whole height of a phone.
- Power: "Fast Charging" above "Maximize Charge".
